Never execute an unknown sample during triage. I'll identify its format statically first.
{"tool": "binary_info", "arguments": {"path": "/cases/loot/sample.bin"}, "why": "identify ELF/PE/Mach-O and parse the header before any deeper RE"}
Then I'd pull strings and symbols. Everything here is static and read-only; strings are UNTRUSTED data, not proof of behaviour — a benign string can be planted and a packed sample hides them.
